            "source_quote": "ἐλεήσαντες οὖν με οἱ ἐπιχώριοι, γυμνὴν ἰδόντες ἐνδύσαντές με τὸ πρῶτον, τὸν βυθὸν ἀνηραύνων, τὰ ἐμὰ ζητοῦντες τέκνα.",
            "english_quote": "The image-checked selected edition prints the nominative singular participle ἀνηραύνων amid plural participles governed by the plural subject οἱ ἐπιχώριοι. This is an apparent agreement irregularity, but the surrounding plural forms make the local people the defensible agent of the search.",
            "issue": "The English translation correctly identifies the local people as searching, but the notes incorrectly characterize the Greek as defective. Here ἀνηραύνων is a contracted third-person plural imperfect, meaning “they were searching,” not a nominative singular participle. It supplies the sentence’s finite verb and agrees with οἱ ἐπιχώριοι. The alleged agreement irregularity and proposed correction are therefore unwarranted.",
            "suggested_revision": "Retain “searched the deep.” Remove the source_issues entry and its proposed_reading “ἀνηραύνοντες.” In the lexical_decisions entry for “τὸν βυθὸν ἀνηραύνων,” replace the claim about a singular participle with an explanation identifying the contracted plural imperfect. This is a correction to the draft’s grammatical analysis, not to the supplied Greek; no additional print verification is required. Submit the revised notes for fresh review.",
